DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The eetthheerrsswwiittcchhccffgg utility is used to configure an Ethernet switch built
     into the system.  eetthheerrsswwiittcchhccffgg accepts a number of options:

     --ff ccoonnttrrooll ffiillee
         Specifies the etherswitch(4) control file that represents the switch
         to be configured.  It defaults to _/_d_e_v_/_e_t_h_e_r_s_w_i_t_c_h_0.
     --mm  When reporting port information, also list available media options
         for that port.
     --vv  Produce more verbose output.  Without this flag, lines that represent
         inactive or empty configuration options are omitted.

   ccoonnffiigg
     The config command provides access to global switch configuration parame‐
     ters.  It support the following commands:

     vvllaann__mmooddee _m_o_d_e  Sets the switch VLAN mode (depends on the hardware).

   pphhyy
     The phy command provides access to the registers of the PHYs attached to
     or integrated into the switch controller.  PHY registers are specified as
     phy.register, where _p_h_y is usually the port number, and _r_e_g_i_s_t_e_r is the
     register number.  Both can be provided as decimal, octal or hexadecimal
     numbers in any of the formats understood by strtol(3).  To set the regis‐
     ter value, use the form instance.register=value.

   ppoorrtt
     The port command selects one of the ports of the switch.  It supports the
     following commands:

     ppvviidd _n_u_m_b_e_r  Sets the default port VID that is used to process incoming
                  frames that are not tagged.
     mmeeddiiaa _m_e_d_i_a_s_p_e_c
                  Specifies the physical media configuration to be configured
                  for a port.
     mmeeddiiaaoopptt _m_e_d_i_a_o_p_t_i_o_n
                  Specifies a list of media options for a port.  See
                  ifconfig(8) for details on mmeeddiiaa and mmeeddiiaaoopptt.
     lleedd _n_u_m_b_e_r _s_t_y_l_e
                  Sets the display style for a given LED.  Available styles
                  are: ddeeffaauulltt (usually flash on activity), oonn, ooffff, and
                  bblliinnkk.  Not all switches will support all styles.

     And the following flags (please note that not all flags are supported by
     all switch drivers):

     aaddddttaagg   Add VLAN tag to each packet sent by the port.
     --aaddddttaagg  Disable the add VLAN tag option.
     ssttrriippttaagg
              Strip the VLAN tags from the packets sent by the port.
     --ssttrriippttaagg
              Disable the strip VLAN tag option.
     ssttrriippttaaggiinnggrreessss
              Strip the VLAN tags from the packets received by the port.
     --ssttrriippttaaggiinnggrreessss
              Disable the strip VLAN tag on ingress option.
     ffiirrssttlloocckk
              This options makes the switch port lock on the first MAC address
              it sees.  After that, usually you need to reset the switch to
              learn different MAC addresses.
     --ffiirrssttlloocckk
              Disable the first lock option.  Note that sometimes you need to
              reset the switch to really disable this option.
     ddrrooppttaaggggeedd
              Drop packets with a VLAN tag.
     --ddrrooppttaaggggeedd
              Disable the drop tagged packets option.
     ddrrooppuunnttaaggggeedd
              Drop packets without a VLAN tag.
     --ddrrooppuunnttaaggggeedd
              Disable the drop untagged packets option.
     ddoouubblleettaagg
              Enable QinQ for the port.
     --ddoouubblleettaagg
              Disable QinQ for the port.
     iinnggrreessss  Enable the ingress filter on the port.
     --iinnggrreessss
              Disable the ingress filter.

   rreegg
     The reg command provides access to the registers of the switch con‐
     troller.

   vvllaannggrroouupp
     The vlangroup command selects one of the VLAN groups for configuration.
     It supports the following commands:

     vvllaann _V_I_D
              Sets the VLAN ID (802.1q VID) for this VLAN group.  Frames
              transmitted on tagged member ports of this group will be tagged
              with this VID.  Incoming frames carrying this tag will be for‐
              warded according to the configuration of this VLAN group.
     mmeemmbbeerrss _p_o_r_t_,_._._.
              Configures which ports are to be a member of this VLAN group.
              The port numbers are given as a comma-separated list.  Each port
              can optionally be followed by “t” to indicate that frames on
              this port are tagged.

FFIILLEESS
